There are four layers of software stack, from layer one to layer 4 sitting next to the one below it.
This four includes:
1. system foundation
2. package managers
3. language runtimes
4. AI/ML libraries

EXPLAINATIONS:
1. System foundation is the foundation, the place  where everything else comes into. it includes OS, shell, editor and the GPU drivers.
system foundation plays the role of standpoint.

a. OS means operating system that handles files and the processes.
b. Shell does the work installation, where commands are been run and scripts lauched.
c. Git trackes changes to one's code, it helps to undo miskes and enables collabrations.
d. Editor is where codes are written.
e. GPU drivers helps training and running of AI models to run fast


2. Package managers plays the role of installers and orangers that fetch libraries and keep projest from crashing each other.
the includes uv, pnpm, cargo and juliaup functions in different ways.
a. UV manages python versions instll libraries such as pytouch, it also replaces pip and venv.
b. pnpm is a package manager for Nodes and javascript
c. Cargo is a building tool for Rust built-in
d. juliaup manages julia versions.

3. Language Runtimes plays the role of code execution.
it function as python3.11+, Node 20+, Rust, uv is written in rust

4. AI/ML libraries plays the role of actual AI work, everything above exist to support it, this includes pytorch, jax and transformers.
a. pytorch it handles tensors and computation on a GPU
b. jax is for large scale training and for research.
c. transformers function as ready made model such as Llama and BERT.
With these libraries one can write math and model architectures and  turns long time of work into few lines of codes.